TelephonyProvider: reload the APN list when the build fingerprint changes.

TelephonyProvider updates its APN database from apns-conf.xml only when ro.build.id
changes. WSA-Next releases of one Android version keep AOSP's build id and differ in
the build number (and so in the fingerprint), so an update never reloaded the list:
the APNs that a release added (MMS through the PC's modem) stayed missing until the
user data was reset. Compare the fingerprint instead; the database is still reloaded
only when the file's checksum has changed.

diff --git a/src/com/android/providers/telephony/TelephonyProvider.java b/src/com/android/providers/telephony/TelephonyProvider.java
index 9e1c189..c6570ee 100644
--- a/src/com/android/providers/telephony/TelephonyProvider.java
+++ b/src/com/android/providers/telephony/TelephonyProvider.java
@@ -3420,7 +3420,10 @@ public class TelephonyProvider extends ContentProvider
         mOpenHelper = new DatabaseHelper(getContext());
         mDefaultSubId = SubscriptionManager.getDefaultSubscriptionId();
         boolean isNewBuild = false;
-        String newBuildId = SystemProperties.get("ro.build.id", null);
+        // WSA-Next: the build fingerprint, which every release changes (its build number); the
+        // build id stays the same between releases of one Android version, so an update would
+        // never reload the APN list.
+        String newBuildId = SystemProperties.get("ro.build.fingerprint", null);
         SharedPreferences sp = getContext().getSharedPreferences(BUILD_ID_FILE,
                 Context.MODE_PRIVATE);
         if (!TextUtils.isEmpty(newBuildId)) {
